-- A shape whose verdict must be INVARIANT under `interface`-declaration order.
--
-- `Sh`'s two impls are ⊑-incomparable and the goal is NOT closed (`[]` leaves an
-- unbound metavariable). This is test/dict_fixtures/s6-2-t4-open-goal-deferred.mdk's
-- shape, plus a second interface so this gate's permuter has two chunks to move.
--
-- Until §6.2 T4's open-goal reject (R-SC3, #1183) this file was a measured NEGATIVE
-- result: its value was decided by `impl`-BLOCK order (`1`, or `2` with the impl
-- blocks swapped) while both interface orderings agreed, showing the two axes were
-- independent. The open goal is now `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE` at `sh` on every
-- ordering of either axis, so what this case grades is that both interface
-- orderings reject the same way.
--
-- Unledgered on purpose, so the gate grades it as invariant and reds if it moves: if
-- a later change makes THIS shape depend on interface order, the fix has introduced
-- an order dependence where there was none. Do not ledger it to make that green.
data Q a b c = Q a b c

interface Sh a where
  sh : a -> Int

interface Tg a where
  tg : a -> Int

impl Sh (Q Int y z) where
  sh _ = 1

impl Sh (Q x Bool z) where
  sh _ = 2

impl Tg (Q Int y z) where
  tg _ = 9

main = println (sh (Q 1 True []))
